WEBVTT

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.650
Hey, look. It's Hakone Academy.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.810
What is he doing at a Chiba race?

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.210
<i>I hear music.</i>

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.420
<i>It's classical music.</i>

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.920
<i>A thrilling symphony.</i>

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:36.220
<i>I finally get to be in a race.</i>

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.560
<i>Thank you, Shinkai-san, Fukutomi-san.</i>

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.630
He's huge!

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.440
He must be at least two meters tall!

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:52.230
<i>I promise I'll beat Onoda Sakamichi.</i>

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:56.950
<b>Minegayama Hill Climb Race</b>

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.950
<i>The total distance of the Minegayama 
Hill Climb is sixteen kilometers!</i>

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:01.020
<i>Beneath this clear autumn sky
 we've been blessed with,</i>

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.030
<i>the riders have started the race!</i>

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.390
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.520
It's the champions, Sohoku!

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:41.030
<i>RIDE.03 Teshima's Ride of the Soul</i>

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:41.370
I was at Mt. Fuji at the Inter-High!

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.720
Imaizumi-kun!

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.390
A giant banner?

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.480
He looked this way!

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.320
What was that?

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.940
Groupies, huh?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.980
Looks like you have more than before.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:57.680
Teshima-san!

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.510
Their support makes us stronger.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.770
Yeah, but they're taking it too far.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.740
Onoda-kun!

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.580
You're so cute!

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:05.590
Huh? What?

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:06.750
Thanks!

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.040
This guy is cute?

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.500
They'll like anyone as long as they win.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:13.420
Onoda!

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:18.300
How's the pace?

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.560
I'm fine.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:25.600
Okay.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.720
Make sure you keep up.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.560
Yes, sir.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.400
What's this? He's huge!

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.520
H-Hey, you're Chiba Minami Middle 
School's Ashikiba, right?

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.800
Harada-san, do you know him?

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.540
Is Hakone Academy trying to scope us out?

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.280
No.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.040
He's here to win.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.580
That's the kind of guy he is!

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.420
Move!

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:03.130
I have business at the front of the pack!

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.010
I haven't raced in a while!

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:09.640
I'm in an awesome mood!

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.390
He's so fast!

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.060
He passed us in a second!

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:19.320
He rhythmically moves his giant 
body back and forth while dancing.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.990
Almost as if he's a metronome.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.400
<i>The Ninth...</i>

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.830
<i>Beethoven's Ninth Symphony.</i>

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.980
<i>Also known as the Choral Symphony.</i>

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:39.000
<i>I'm so clichéd. It's not 
even the end of the year.</i>

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.470
<i>I'd been placed under house arrest indefinitely.</i>

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:48.760
<i>But a race... now, I'm riding in a race!</i>

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.890
<i>I will take first place.</i>

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:53.990
<i>First place...</i>

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.030
<i>...is righteous!</i>

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.280
Teshima-san, there's something bothering me.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:09.640
There's a Hakone Academy second-year 
named Ashikiba riding in the race.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:11.530
I saw his name on the participant list.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:13.120
What? Hakone Academy?

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.370
Seems that way.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.220
You're a second-year, too.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.750
Do you know him, Teshima-san?

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.240
Yeah, I know him well.

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:23.800
We used to ride on the same team.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:31.260
<i>The symphony's playing inside my head.</i>

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:35.230
<i>I don't know who said it,
but someone called the way I ride...</i>

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:33.890
He's so fast!

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:36.980
He's coming.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:40.560
<i>Metronome Dancing!</i>

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:42.940
Hakone Academy!

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:45.720
So this is the second-year, Ashikiba.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.570
He's huge. He's bigger than me!

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:54.370
I caught up, Sohoku High.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:59.380
<i>He's not short of breath,
even though he rode up from the back.</i>

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.750
<i>And what's with his frame?</i>

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:07.480
<i>Like shoes, frames are designed 
to match the size of your body.</i>

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:13.510
<i>But no matter how large the frame gets, 
the size of the tires doesn't change.</i>

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.770
<i>This guy's frame...</i>

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.050
<i>I've never seen anything so huge.</i>

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:22.320
<i>It makes his tires look smaller.</i>

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.650
<i>It's like he's riding a small-wheeled bike.</i>

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:29.280
So you're Onoda.

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:32.030
Yes.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:38.600
So you're Onoda.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.370
<i>He corrected himself!</i>

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:42.410
I've heard about you.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:47.070
You'll race up any hill with 
your extraordinary cadence.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:48.380
<i>And he's pretending he didn't!</i>

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.510
And you're another first-year...

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:52.690
Yeah.

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:54.510
The red bean, Naruko.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.270
<i>He got it wrong with that 
smug look on his face!</i>

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.230
I've heard about you.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.760
<i>There's nothing red about me...</i>

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:04.120
By climbing with your exceptional 
grit and sprinter's legs,

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.420
<i>Can't he tell by looking?</i>

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:06.750
you caught up to Hakone Academy.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:07.530
<i>Imaizumi-kun doesn't seem 
like a bean to me.</i>

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:11.110
Then you dropped out of the 
race in heroic fashion.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.650
<i>It's hard to call him out since he's older.</i>

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.410
<i>Maybe this guy's just an airhead?</i>

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:14.770
<i>I kind of feel bad for him.</i>

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:19.320
Um, can I offer a correction?

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.000
Huh? Yeah, go ahead.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:22.880
No, wait.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.120
I haven't said anything 
that needs correcting.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:27.590
<i>What?</i>

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.260
<i>I can't tell him now!</i>

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:32.620
Sohoku has another first-year.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.640
<i>Imaizumi-kun's starting to get mad.</i>

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.570
I know.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.520
Don't underestimate Hakone 
Academy's information network.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:41.350
It's me.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.290
The silky-haired Sugimoto Terufumi.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:46.500
That's right, Sugimoto Teru...

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.650
Hello!

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:53.910
<i>I worked pretty hard at the Inter-High...</i>

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.290
<i>This is a real shock.</i>

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.990
Did Sohoku not bring all their members?

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:01.290
Ashikiba!

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.460
How have you been?

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:06.390
Good.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:10.040
Are you still playing the piano?

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:12.200
Sometimes.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.710
I heard you joined Hakone Academy.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.430
I passed their exam.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.750
We used to ride together a lot.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:21.950
Yeah.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.060
Jun-chan...

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:26.710
Shikiba...

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:35.410
Shikiba, that's amazing.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.780
Since my fingers are so long,
they said I'd be good at the piano.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:41.990
I can play J-Pop songs, too, like Hira Ken.

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:43.040
Seriously?

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:54.980
Do you know what a road bike is?

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:57.680
Yeah, those thin ones.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:00.260
Wow.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:05.450
I wanted to try it out after watching a DVD.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:08.230
Shikiba, want to join me?

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:10.710
It's so cool.

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:13.320
It's like an instrument.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:15.820
It's so thin and shiny.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.320
There's nothing unnecessary on it.

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:20.870
I wonder if it makes a nice sound.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:25.960
The ratchets on the wheels will 
send shivers down your spine.

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:31.080
This sound, this energy...

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.140
This vibration!

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.300
This is amazing.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:36.050
It truly is an instrument!

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:41.470
I'm thinking about doing 
this pretty seriously.

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:43.720
I'm going to race internationally.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:45.980
Internationally?

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:48.640
Just kidding.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:51.770
Are you gonna laugh because
 I'm dreaming too big?

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:53.860
Of course not.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.270
That's amazing. It's cool.

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:57.490
You have my support.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:02.200
Let's ride!

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.270
I'll become the best in the world!

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:06.660
Jun-chan!

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.050
Let's become the best together.

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:11.830
You'll be right there with me.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:15.670
Jun-chan...

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.050
Shikiba.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:21.470
Honestly, I was shaken when 
I saw the participant list...

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:25.720
When I learned you were 
on Hakone Academy's team.

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:30.340
When I heard you became 
the captain of Sohoku,

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:34.110
I thought you were worthy of the position.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:40.570
I knew you were good enough to do it.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:47.250
Do you remember how I told you 
we'd become champions together?

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.070
Yeah, of course.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:55.020
But I'm the captain of Sohoku now.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.560
In other words, their pillar.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:11:02.590
Now I have to fight against you 
and Hakone Academy, Ashikiba!

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.050
Same here...

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.980
Since I'm Hakone Academy's next ace.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.990
<i>Their next ace?</i>

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:20.090
<i>Hakone Academy second-year Ashikiba...</i>

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:24.660
<i>This guy will be their ace next year?</i>

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:31.060
<i>Since he's so tall, the distance from his hip joint 
to his knees is exceptionally long.</i>

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:33.960
<i>Every time he turns the pedals, 
I can hear the wind whistle.</i>

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:36.880
<i>No, wait! It wasn't making 
that sound a minute ago.</i>

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:41.590
<i>Which means he's started 
pedaling at full power.</i>

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.800
There's so much pressure.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:47.680
Shikiba...

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:48.820
Jun-chan...

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:53.450
Jun-chan, I don't want to 
crush the team you made.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.610
I wish I could join it instead.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:12:01.370
But I owe the seniors of Hakone Academy...

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:05.740
I told them I would win this race!

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.850
How is he dancing like that?

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:08.990
His body's swaying back and forth!

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:10.670
He's accelerating so quickly!

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:12.000
In just a single step, too!

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.730
Thanks for the ride.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:23.930
Old man, your elbows and ass are in the way!

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.730
What are you complaining about?

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:26.720
Look at Aoyagi.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:29.780
He's sitting quietly, without saying a word.

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:31.680
He never says anything!

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:34.100
I'm sitting quietly, too.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:35.960
You're just too big!

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:36.830
You boys sure make a lot of noise.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:37.660
Shut up! You're just...

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:38.700
<i>Teshima...</i>

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:43.210
<i>It's hard to imagine Hakone Academy would send
 someone just to scope out the competition.</i>

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:45.470
<i>They'll be going for the win.</i>

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:47.290
<i>Expect them to challenge us.</i>

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.790
<i>Onoda's not doing well.</i>

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:56.030
<i>He switched to a new bike, but he's 
still only drawing out 30% of his power.</i>

00:12:56.990 --> 00:13:00.340
<i>Probably because of Makishima.</i>

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:06.050
<i>As a fellow climber, he provided 
moral support, and he quit the club early.</i>

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:09.450
<i>But regretting that forever 
won't change anything.</i>

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:13.250
<i>He has to move forward despite it.
That's part of road racing.</i>

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:16.910
<i>If you don't move forward, 
you'll be left behind.</i>

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:19.230
Kinjou-kun,

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:23.920
as their former captain, which of the 
Sohoku members do you think will win?

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:25.310
Will it be Onoda-kun again?

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:26.890
Or Imaizumi-kun?

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:28.170
I don't know.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.440
Personally speaking,

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:37.230
I think the Hakone Academy second-year 
on the participant list could win.

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:45.720
I think this race could determine the 
future of Sohoku's new generation.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.700
But we're the champions.

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:50.180
Champions would never...

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:57.480
Damn it.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:01.000
I ran from the pack to try to win,
 but someone's catching up.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.690
And he's huge!

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.090
There's someone right behind him.

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:05.940
It's Sohoku.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:08.070
Their captain, Teshima!

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.070
Ashikiba!

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:12.770
<i>Teshima-san is fast!</i>

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:17.580
<i>We couldn't even respond, but he reacted 
instantly and kept up with him.</i>

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:20.960
<i>The Teshima-san I know would've already...</i>

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:22.570
<i>What is this?</i>

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:25.960
<i>He's nothing like he was 
at the training camp.</i>

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:29.180
<i>Has he always been this fast?</i>

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:44.580
Jun-chan!

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:45.780
Shikiba!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.410
We're the champions!

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.740
We won't let you take the Minegayama title!

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:53.280
You really are amazing, Jun-chan!

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.620
The seniors who scoped out
 the CSC training camp

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.710
said second-year Teshima was nothing special.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:04.270
I couldn't tell them, but I 
didn't think that was possible.

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:07.130
I'll make them revise their evaluation later.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:08.880
Are you ready to go?

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:13.090
There's only four kilometers left.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.090
<b>Distance to Finish Line</b>

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:18.980
We used to climb together a lot and 
get frustrated when we had to stop.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.600
<b>Ahead</b>

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:21.600
On Minegayama's iconic...

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.520
Kabesaka!

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:28.640
Amazing.

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:33.280
I can hear Beethoven's Fifth 
playing inside my head!

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:41.000
<i>Ashikiba's good.</i>

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:45.860
<i>He's gotten way better since middle school.</i>

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:47.710
<i>He's certainly on the level of an ace.</i>

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:49.880
<i>He could still go harder.</i>

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:53.800
<i>But I'm Sohoku's captain!</i>

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:57.970
<i>I can't let him pull away!</i>

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:06.020
<i>Naruko lost speed on this hill 
during the first-year race.</i>

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:11.320
<i>Why do I feel so hot?</i>

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:14.500
<i>Just how hard did he work?</i>

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:20.650
<i>The way Teshima-san is riding is enchanting.</i>

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:24.750
T-Teshima-san is amazing.

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:26.170
<i>Onoda...</i>

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:28.500
He's amazing.

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:31.340
Amazing!

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:37.780
<i>Ashikiba, you always overestimate me.</i>

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:40.670
<i>"You're amazing, Jun-chan. You're worthy."</i>

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:43.690
<i>It makes me happy to hear that,
but it's just not true.</i>

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:45.770
<i>I'm weak.</i>

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:50.300
<i>I'm clinging to my handlebars, 
hanging onto legs that feel like</i>

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:54.740
<i>they're about to stop, and my heart's 
beating out of my chest.</i>

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:58.040
<i>Honestly, I'm not on your level.</i>

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:01.800
<i>But Ashikiba, I won't lose!</i>

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:03.250
<i>Because I'm...</i>

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:06.210
<i>The captain of Sohoku!</i>

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:07.860
Two kilometers left!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:14.050
Beethoven's Fifth won't stop playing!

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:21.100
Metronome Dancing! This is it!

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:23.890
<i>Did I reach my limit?</i>

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:26.430
<i>Keep fighting, Junta!</i>

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:31.400
<i>You're here because Makishima-san 
told you to climb!</i>

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.830
Shikiba!

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:43.200
He caught up!

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.100
You caught up again.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:48.000
Jun-chan, you really are amazing.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.330
That Hakone Academy guy is huge!

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:51.450
I've never seen him before!

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:52.490
Who is he?

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:54.710
<i>Classmates?</i>

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:57.760
Yeah, from middle school.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:01.280
He's tall and kind.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:03.720
He's always complimenting other people.

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:06.430
We used to ride together a lot.

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:10.360
I've never told you about him before.

00:18:10.850 --> 00:18:12.500
Your teammate, then?

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:15.680
We promised to become champions together.

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.240
But...

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.640
Unfortunately, today he's my opponent.

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:24.020
<i>A battle against a friend...</i>

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.780
<i>He's steeled his resolve as the new captain.</i>

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:31.380
<i>But I can tell...</i>

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:35.830
<i>Junta's approaching his limit.</i>

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:53.240
He's still hanging on.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.270
Perm head!

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:56.660
1.5 kilometers left.

00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:59.640
Sorry, Teshima-san.

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:03.660
Honestly, I didn't think much of you.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.160
Look at this, old man.

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:09.710
The gutsy way he's riding 
is making my hands shake.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:11.960
Of course it is.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:14.840
I'm the one who trained Teshima and Aoyagi.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:18.200
You didn't teach them how to climb.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:21.370
He might just make it to 
the finish line like this.

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:22.250
He can't.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:28.330
Like Makishima said, Teshima has 
no talent or instinct for climbing.

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:31.430
When it comes to climbing, he's mediocre.

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:33.400
And mediocre riders have their limits.

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:36.150
Why would you say that, Kinjou-san?

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.690
Did he not impress you?

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.430
You should be cheering him on!

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:41.150
Naruko...

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:45.030
Are you saying Sohoku's going to lose 
to that lanky Hakone Academy guy?

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:48.370
No, not necessarily.

00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:55.040
Teshima's riding is affecting them 
the same way it affected you.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.630
More than we ever did.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:05.910
The two riding behind Teshima are 
feeling his passionate vibrations.

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:10.020
I'm shaking. I'm on fire.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.560
How can he ride like that?

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:14.200
How can he keep up?

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.060
Imaizumi-kun...

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:21.900
I want to ride all out and 
catch up to Teshima-san!

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:26.310
<i>Onoda!</i>

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:27.780
<i>Imaizumi...</i>

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:33.210
If... If Onoda says he wants
to attack during the race...

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.420
gently push him forward.

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:40.170
Imaizumi-kun!

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.910
There's no need to hold back.

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:47.430
Teshima-san will accept you with open arms.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:53.770
If you want to catch up to him,
charge straight ahead...

00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:57.960
Onoda Sakamichi!

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:58.810
Got it!

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:03.570
Onoda-kun's going for it!

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:05.900
He's trying to catch up.

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:07.990
Hotshot sent Onoda-kun off.

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:10.690
Teshima's an average rider.

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:14.500
But that's why he moves 
the people around him.

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:17.380
And those vibrations become their strength.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:21.400
That power is transmitted to his teammates.

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:27.890
Teshima, is that how you captain your team?

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:29.390
Teshima-san!

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:33.810
<i>Onoda!</i>

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:37.190
Don't worry, Naruko.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:40.430
The race isn't over yet.

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:17.580
You're so cute!

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:18.670
Huh? What?

00:23:18.670 --> 00:23:19.490
Thanks!

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:26.620
Teshima-san, I think you're, uh...

00:23:26.620 --> 00:23:28.210
I think you're handsome.

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:30.280
Really?

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:34.720
Imaizumi, I'll call you "Elite" 
for the rest of the week.

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>NEXT RIDE The Fastest Man on Minegayama</i>

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:44.980
